  "notes": "{高|たか}める is a transitive ichidan verb meaning to raise, elevate, or enhance.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {高|たか}まる (intransitive, to rise/increase)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{高|たか}めている indicates an ongoing effort to improve or elevate something.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {能力|のうりょく}を{高|たか}める: to improve abilities\n- {技術|ぎじゅつ}を{高|たか}める: to enhance skills\n- {質|しつ}を{高|たか}める: to improve quality\n- {効率|こうりつ}を{高|たか}める: to increase efficiency\n- {意識|いしき}を{高|たか}める: to raise awareness\n- {士気|しき}を{高|たか}める: to boost morale\n- {声|こえ}を{高|たか}める: to raise one's voice\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used in business and self-improvement contexts. The pair {高|たか}まる describes something rising on its own: {期待|きたい}が{高|たか}まる (expectations rise).",
